Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-15-2001||09:37 PM||||As you may remember, I bought a DVD player in Florida, and after 2-3 movies, it just wouldn't turn on anymore. So after contacting Toshiba of Canada, they cannot do anything and I would have to contact T of America. I phoned them, constantly, and NO ONE would answer the phone. So I looked up a list of there service stations, and phoned one in buffalo, and they said theyw ould probably have to charge me to fix it (I don't want it fixed, I want a new one!) but apparently the only way to get a new one is to bring it back to the store I bought it from, IN FLORIDA! After sending numerous emails to Toshiba of America (they never wrote back for awhile) I finally got one back saying "Once the player has crossed the border into Canada, you have voided the warranty" WHat the hell is that?! Looks like on Tuesday I'm driving down to buffalo to get a 6 hour old dvd player repaired.. Last time I ever buy anything Toshiba made. There customer service and appreciation is disgusting.||||reg||1
